{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "advection_1d_ppm_periodic",
    "description": "MMS driver: 1-D linear advection u_t = -c u_x on the periodic unit interval [0, 1], discretized by grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/ppm_D_periodic (Piecewise Parabolic Method, Colella-Woodward 1984; conservative finite-volume, semi-discrete method-of-lines flux, non-negative speed). Exact solution u(x,t) = sin(2 pi (x - c t)) transported at speed c with no change of shape, so no forcing term is required. FLUX FORM: the rule uses the semi-discrete reconstructed-edge PPM flux F_{i+1/2} = qr_lim(cell i) (the CW84-limited right edge of the upwind cell), not the fully-discrete Courant-integral flux, because the ESS simulate() pathway is method-of-lines (the rule provides only D(u,x); the ODE integrator owns dt) -- see the rule file for the full rationale. OBSERVED ORDER (honest): PPM is nominally 3rd order (parabolic reconstruction) and the unlimited flux-difference is exactly 4th-order central, but the original CW84 monotonicity limiter still clips the two smooth extrema of the sine (the classic smooth-extremum clipping of the 1984 limiter), flattening the parabola there to first order. The global order is therefore sub-nominal and norm-dependent -- about 1.7 in L2 and 1.3 in Linf over N=16..128; the convergence gate (tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_ppm_periodic) asserts the honestly-observed order, NOT the nominal 3. CONSERVATION: the flux-difference telescopes on the periodic ring and neighbouring cells share the identical float face flux, so sum(u) (hence mean(u)) is preserved to the bit -- the t=0.1 mean-conservation assertion pins this. The grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0, 1]: x0 = 0 (parameter) and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing the extent by the metaparameter name N, esm-spec 9.7.6, so the convergence sweep's loader-API rebinding of N keeps dx consistent) resolve the rule body's free dx at evaluation. Initial condition and test references spell the grid's index-to-coordinate conversion x_i = x0 + (i - 1/2) dx = 0 + (i - 1/2)(1/N) inline with load-foldable scalars, not via the free-name x_coord template: the official 6.6.5/ic build-time cellwise evaluation is scope-free (model parameters/observeds are not in scope there).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "equation:advection",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Colella, P., & Woodward, P. R. (1984). The Piecewise Parabolic Method (PPM) for gas-dynamical simulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 54(1), 174-201.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(84)90143-8"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2002). Finite Volume Methods for Hyperbolic Problems. Cambridge University Press. Chapter 6 (high-resolution methods) and Chapter 9 (systems)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "AdvectionPPM": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/ppm_D_periodic.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Advected tracer field over the x index set."
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Constant transport speed (non-negative; the PPM upwind flux assumes flow in +x)."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter (re-exported up the import chain), substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "sin",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  6.283185307179586,
                  {
                    "op": "faq",
                    "output_idx": [
                      "i"
                    ],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": {
                      "i": {
                        "from": "x"
                      }
                    },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        0,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "c"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "D",
                "args": [
                  "u"
                ],
                "wrt": "x"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "N"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_transport",
          "description": "Exact solution u(x,t) = sin(2 pi (x - c t)) with c = 1. Derivation: u_t = -2 pi c cos(2 pi (x - c t)) = -c u_x exactly, periodic on [0,1]; no forcing term. References evaluate at the cell centers x_i = x0 + (i - 1/2) dx = 0 + (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (1-based index space; build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (L2_error 0 within 1e-9). The t=0.1 L2_error assertion bounds the PPM transport error (about 5e-4 relative L2 at the default N=64, well under the 0.01 cap, which holds across the convergence sweep). The t=0.1 mean assertion pins EXACT conservation: the semi-discrete PPM flux-difference telescopes on the periodic ring, so mean(u) is preserved to the bit at its analytic value 0 (the discrete sine has zero mean over the full period). Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_ppm_periodic/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.1
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.283185307179586,
                      {
                        "op": "faq",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.01
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.283185307179586,
                      {
                        "op": "-",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "faq",
                            "output_idx": [
                              "i"
                            ],
                            "args": [],
                            "ranges": {
                              "i": {
                                "from": "x"
                              }
                            },
                            "expr": {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                0,
                                {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "-",
                                      "args": [
                                        "i",
                                        0.5
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "op": "/",
                                      "args": [
                                        1,
                                        "N"
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          },
                          0.1
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "mean"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
